{"school":{"dbn":"30Q204","name":"I.S. 204 Oliver W. Holmes","boro":"Queens","district":"30","district_label":"District 30","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":266,"enrollment_year":"2025-26","address":"36-41 28 STREET, QUEENS, NY 11106","phone":"718-335-7500","website":"www.owhschool.weebly.com","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/70495","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"The school mission at OWH is to prepare every student for excellence through rigorous academics. At OWH we strive to create a student-centered environment in which students embody our school's core values (Growth Mindset, Honesty, Leadership, & Perseverance) by promoting student achievement and college and career readiness. The OWH multi-faceted curricula infuses school-wide enrichment and gifted and talented methodologies, which are tailored to meet the needs of all students by incorporating highly engaging interdisciplinary activities throughout all standards based curricular topics while adhering to all academic policy requirements. Specialized programs at OWH include: : Spanish Dual Language, STEM Magnet, NEST ASD, Bilingual Special Education, & ACES.  Student Activities at OWH include: Athletic Teams (Basketball, Flag-Football, Fitness Club, Soccer, & Volleyball), ARISTA Junior Honor's Society, Band, Chess Club, College Access for All, Comfort Dog, ESports Team, Green Team, Mouse Squad, Robotics, School Wellness, Service Learning, STEM Lab (3D Printing, Golf Simulator, Hydroponics Lab, Robotics, Flight Simulator, & Virtual Reality Goggles), Student Council, Student Led Conferences, Yearbook, & UN Junior Ambassadors. School Partnerships include: Greater Ridgewood Youth Council Beacon/21st Century After-School Program, CHAMPS Fitness, CUNY Creative Arts, Intrepid Museum, Museum of Moving Image, Noguchi Museum, NYC Outward Bound, & Urban Advantage.","start_time":"08:00am","e